scene functions

// ═══════════════════ FUNCTIONS & PROCEDURES ═══════════════════
// The witness for `func` — both of the things that word means, in one scene.
//
//   func f(a, b) { return <expr> }    EXPRESSION function. The call is INLINED
//                                     into the expression at compile time, so
//                                     it works anywhere an expression works:
//                                     an assignment, an {interpolation}, an
//                                     `if`, a choice `expr=`. No recursion.
//   func p(a) { <commands> }          PROCEDURE. Lowered to call/return and
//                                     invoked as a statement on its own line.
//
// A lighthouse keeper does the evening arithmetic. Every number on screen comes
// out of a `func`, so if the lowering ever breaks again this scene shows zeros
// and the compile gate goes red.

// ─── Expression functions ───────────────────────────────────────────────
// One-liner form: the body is a single `return <expr>`.
func fuel_cost(hours) { return 3 * hours + 2 }

// Multi-line form, same meaning.
func bonus(nights, rate) {
  return floor(nights * rate / 10)
}

// They may call each other — the compiler inlines the whole chain.
func payout(nights, rate, hours) { return bonus(nights, rate) - fuel_cost(hours) }

// ─── A procedure ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The body is COMMANDS, so it runs as a statement. Arguments bind to ordinary
// variables just before the jump (no frames — so no recursion here either).
func log_entry(what, amount) {
  Keeper: {what} — {amount} shillings.
}

nights = 6
rate = 25
hours = 4
purse = 0

bg /content/bg/lighthouse.jpg
text hud x=4 y=6 size=38 color=#cfe8ff «💰{purse}  🌙{nights}  ⛽{fuel_cost(hours)}»

The lamp is trimmed. The ledger is not.

// A call inside an assignment …
purse = purse + payout(nights, rate, hours)
// … inside an interpolation …
Keeper: {nights} nights at {rate}, minus {fuel_cost(hours)} for the oil.
// … and inside a condition.
if payout(nights, rate, hours) > 0 -> solvent
-> short

:solvent
log_entry("Ledger", purse)
The keeper signs the page.
-> ledger

:short
log_entry("Debt", purse)
The keeper leaves the page unsigned.
-> ledger

:ledger
- 🔢 Count one more night -> recount
- 💰 Bank the bonus ({bonus(nights, rate)}) -> bank expr="bonus(nights, rate) > 5"
- 📕 Close the book -> done

:recount
// Arguments are expressions in their own right.
extra = bonus(nights + 1, rate)
Keeper: One more night would add {extra}.
-> done

:bank
purse = purse + bonus(nights, rate)
log_entry("Bonus", purse)
-> done

:done
text hud hide
The lamp turns, and the coast keeps its distance.
goto __end
